//
// SMU Verilator coverage scope. Passed to Verilator at compile time from
// [coverage.verilator].build_args in smu_sim_cfg.toml, so what it drops never
// enters the coverage database. Edit then `--rebuild`.
//
// Same compile-time rule SEP measured (hw/sys/sep/dv/cov/config/vcs/README.md):
// a report-time filter prunes the report pages and still grades the whole
// database.
//
// The rule for an integration level is that each level grades what it owns.
// SMU instantiates SMC, DTP and SEP, each of which has its own DV package and
// its own coverage; grading them again here would attribute their holes to
// SMU and hide SMU's own interconnect inside a denominator two orders of
// magnitude larger.
//
// GLOB NOTE: the pattern is matched against the path as Verilator OPENED the
// file, not the absolute path it records in the generated code, and
// `+incdir+`-resolved files are opened relative. Never put a `/` straight
// after the leading `*` -- `*vendor/*` matches both forms, `*/vendor/*`
// matches only the absolute one and silently leaves the rest instrumented.
//
// DO NOT add hw/sys/smu/dv/cov/sv/* here. Those files carry the
// OCAH_FCOV_COVER points that populate the `user` metric family.

`verilator_config

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Testbench code.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
coverage_off -file "*hw/sys/smu/dv/tb/tb_top.sv"
coverage_off -file "*hw/sys/smu/dv/tb/tb_wrapper_top.sv"
coverage_off -file "*hw/sys/smu/dv/tb/smu_tb_if.sv"
coverage_off -file "*hw/sys/smu/dv/tb/smu_axi_out_sim_slave.sv"

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Subsystems that carry their own DV package and their own coverage.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
coverage_off -file "*hw/sys/smc/*"
coverage_off -file "*hw/sys/dtp/*"
coverage_off -file "*hw/sys/sep/*"

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Third-party and generated RTL, and the IP blocks the subsystems integrate.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
coverage_off -file "*vendor/*"
coverage_off -file "*chipyard_generated_files/*"
coverage_off -file "*hw/ip/*"
coverage_off -file "*hw/common/*"

// KNOWN GAP. This file takes the toggle denominator from 1350556 sites to
// 19611, but 18591 of what remains is still vendored: axi_lite_demux.sv
// (12886) and the tt-hw-debug generic_dff family (5705). Every one of those
// sites sits under `.u_smc` or `.u_dtp` -- none is under SMU's own crossbar
// -- so the intent is unambiguous and only the mechanism falls short. No file
// pattern reaches them: `*vendor/*`, `*pulp-platform/*`, `*tt-hw-debug/*` and
// the bare `*axi_lite_demux.sv` / `*generic_dff.sv` forms were each built and
// counted, on this DUT and on SMC, and every one left the numbers unchanged.
// Do not add those patterns back -- they look like scope and do nothing.
//
// What is left after this file: 1020 of 19611 sites (5.2%) are SMU's own
// smu.sv. Closing the rest needs a hierarchy selector, which `coverage_off`
// does not have and the coverage policy does; cov/config/verilator/
// coverage_policy.toml records the two selectors to use and why they cannot
// be written until a run produces the database counts they must match.
